<title>USA: Wausau Paper sees stable pulp pricing.</title>
<headline>Wausau Paper sees stable pulp pricing.</headline>
<dateline>WAUSAU, Wis. 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wausau Paper Mills Co said &quot;market fundamentals in the pulp industry point toward relatively stable pricing.&quot;</p>
<p>Chief executive Daniel King said, &quot;I'm confident that the momentum of the past two quarters will continue into fiscal 1997 providing a foundation for additional growth in the years ahead.&quot;</p>
<p>Shares in the paper company were up 1 to 20-1/2 after it reported fourth-quarter earnings of $0.36 per share, up from $0.19 per share a year ago.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
